    "title": "Lexington police looking for suspect connected to 2024 Pasadena Drive robbery - NewsBreak",
    "text": "LEXINGTON, Ky. ( FOX 56 ) — Bluegrass Crime Stoppers is asking for help with their crime of the week. Police said around 11:48 a.m. on Dec. 27, officers responded to a robbery on Pasadena Drive. Witnesses said the suspect handed a note to the teller, threatening harm if cash wasn’t given.\nHe took off on foot. The suspect is described as a Black man wearing a green hoodie, black pants, and black shoes. Anyone with information is asked to call the Lexington Police Department at (859) 258-3600. Anonymous tips can be submitted to Bluegrass Crime Stoppers by calling (859) 253-2020, online at bluegrasscrimestoppers.com , or through the P3 Tips available app at p3tips.com . For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 56 News.",
